S140 LRC14 C27 -> q=3 UNITAL BLOCK-LIFT SYNTHESIS
==============================================================================
[1] Assumption challenge / quotient declaration
  considered vertices:
    runners, C27 residues, antipodal shells, hole/double statuses,
    AP/GW labels, q=3 unital points, unital 4-blocks, branch-local
    charts, S138 two-hole obligations, and S139 affine-depth packets.
  chosen predicates:
    raw test: can marked residue packets be simultaneous q=3 blocks?
    calibrated test: what unique block completes each labelled pair?
  quotient preserves:
    C27 hole/double shell pair, branch label, lambda=1 incidence,
    AP/GW anchor visibility, and transfer-component intersections.
  quotient destroys:
    exact time geometry, canonical S8 symmetry, and within-shell
    orientation beyond the declared antipodal pair.
  challenged assumption:
    one unital chart should contain all low-frontier transfers.  The
    raw lift says no; branch-local charts and calibrated completions work.

[2] q=3 Hermitian unital sanity
  GF(9) model: w^2=-1 over F3; Hermitian equation x^4+y^4+z^4=0.
  projective unital points=28
  non-tangent 4-point blocks=63
  line intersection histogram={1: 28, 4: 63}
  block_size_hist={4: 63}
  point_replication_hist={9: 28}
  pair_to_block entries=378 expected=378
  secant pair multiplicity per block={6: 63}
  block intersection histogram={0: 945, 1: 1008}
  readout: two distinct unital blocks never share two points.

[3] Raw C27 residue-pair block model
  GW  GW H12->D3         branch=tight-floor          block=(3, 12, 15, 24)
  K33 K33 H12->D9        branch=K33-unit-excess      block=(9, 12, 15, 18)
  P10 petal H10->D7      branch=C27-petal-two-block  block=(7, 10, 17, 20)
  P13 petal H13->D1      branch=C27-petal-two-block  block=(1, 13, 14, 26)
  simultaneous low-frontier repeated pairs={(12, 15): 2}
  obstruction:
    GW and K33 both contain the C27 hole pair (12,15).  Since a q=3
    unital has lambda=1, those two packets cannot both be blocks in
    one unital chart under the raw residue-pair lift.

[4] Global AP/GW-label block model
  GW  block=('AP', 'D3', 'GW', 'H12')
  K33 block=('AP', 'D9', 'GW', 'H12')
  P10 block=('AP', 'D7', 'GW', 'H10')
  P13 block=('AP', 'D1', 'GW', 'H13')
  repeated pairs={('AP', 'GW'): 4, ('AP', 'H12'): 2, ('GW', 'H12'): 2}
  readout:
    treating AP and GW as two global points in every transfer block
    repeats the pair (AP,GW).  AP/GW must be chart labels, branch
    colors, or a single calibrated anchor, not universal vertices.

