[8] Verdict / POKE contribution
  Negative global result:
    the raw C27 residue-pair lift cannot put GW H12->D3 and K33
    H12->D9 into the same q=3 unital, because the C27 pair (12,15)
    would occur in two different blocks.
  Positive local result:
    each branch separately embeds into the q=3 unital incidence design,
    and the S138 genuine two-hole rows lift as two-block splices.
  Calibrated pair-completion result:
    after AP/GW labels are attached to one Hermitian unital, each marked
    pair has a unique completion; GW is the AP/GW anchor, and the
    K33/petal near splice forms AP/GW--H12--near/K33--D9--petal10.
  Proof-use refinement:
    use the unital as a branch-local pair-unique chart and POKE forum
    for transfer packets, not as scalar evidence or a universal atlas.
